   "source": [
    "### 13. Constrained Maximum Likelihood Estimation\n",
    "Likelihood: $L(\\theta) = \\theta^k (1-\\theta)^{n-k}$.\n",
    "Unconstrained MLE is $\\hat{\\theta}_{MLE} = k/n$.\n",
    "Due to convexity, the constrained MLE under $0.2 \\le \\theta \\le 0.8$ is simply the projection of $k/n$ onto the interval $[0.2, 0.8]$:\n",
    "$$\\hat{\\theta}_{constrained} = \\text{clip}\\left(\\frac{k}{n}, 0.2, 0.8\\right)$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def constrained_mle(k, n):\n",
    "    unconstrained = k / n\n",
    "    return np.clip(unconstrained, 0.2, 0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"MLE for 1 head out of 10 flips:\", constrained_mle(1, 10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 14. K-Means Clustering as Non-Convex Optimization\n",
    "K-Means objective function is:\n",
    "$$J = \\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{k=1}^K r_{ik} \\|x_i - \\mu_k\\|^2$$\n",
    "where $r_{ik} \\in \\{0, 1\\}$ is 1 if data point $i$ belongs to cluster $k$.\n",
    "This objective is non-convex due to the discrete indicator variables $r_{ik}$. Lloyd's algorithm alternates between:\n",
    "1. **E-step (assignment)**: Optimize $r_{ik}$ holding $\\mu_k$ fixed (assign each point to the closest centroid).\n",
    "2. **M-step (update)**: Optimize $\\mu_k$ holding $r_{ik}$ fixed (compute the mean of each cluster).\n",
    "This coordinate descent guarantees decrease of the objective, but can get stuck in local minima."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
